Re-researched from scratch on 2026-09-27. Searched the public web for `gpt-live-1-astra`, `gpt live 1 astra`, and OpenAI realtime/live voice model variants:

- **Zero search results** for the exact slug on DuckDuckGo web search (2026-09-27).
- No OpenAI newsroom post, docs page, or model listing references this ID. OpenAI's realtime voice line (verified during the same session) is `gpt-realtime` → `gpt-realtime-2` (Nov 2025) → `gpt-realtime-2.1` / `2.1-mini` (2026-07-06), plus minute-metered companions `GPT-Realtime-Translate` / `GPT-Realtime-Whisper`; no "Live" or "Astra" product exists on that surface. ("Astra" nomenclature belongs to Google's Project Astra / Gemini Live line, not OpenAI.)
- No benchmark page (BenchLM, Artificial Analysis, llm-stats) lists this model.
- No Zen/model listing evidence found for an `astra` realtime ID.

**Conclusion:** zero verified public benchmark numbers — and no verifiable evidence the model exists at all under this name. Per RULES.md / research.md self-exclusion, no scored `.md` is written. All template score rows would read `no verified public score found`.

